    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Six-month review of cyclic vomiting syndrome. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Darwin returns after three months at amitriptyline 75 mg at bedtime. He has had one episode in that time, three weeks ago, after an overnight journey with little sleep. He used the sumatriptan spray and an ondansetron tablet at the first nausea and trembling, lay down in a dark room, and was well again within about four hours, without vomiting more than twice. He has had no emergency visits. The dry mouth persists, the constipation is better with more fluid and fiber, and the morning grogginess has faded. He walks most days, practices the relaxation breathing most evenings, and has accepted more invitations than in the spring. He still has some wind between episodes, which troubles him less. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medicine</td><td>Amitriptyline 75 mg at bedtime for three months at the target dose</td></tr><tr><td>Episodes</td><td>One brief episode in three months, after overnight travel, aborted within about four hours</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>Dry mouth; constipation improved; grogginess gone</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Working most days; going out more</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Wind between episodes, less troublesome; one brief episode; constipation improved</td></tr><tr><td>Ears, nose, mouth, and throat</td><td>Positive</td><td>Dry mouth</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Negative</td><td>No palpitations outside the prodrome; no fainting</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Negative</td><td>Mood good; worry about episodes much less; no thoughts of self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

